cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. Cite the
  tagged release your results came from, not the default branch.
title: "Climate Trust Network (CTN): an IoT-to-blockchain prototype for verifiable renewable-energy MRV"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jha
    given-names: Aditya
    email: aqui.adi.j@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent researcher, Patna, India
repository-code: "https://github.com/aquiadi/ctn-mvp-complete"
url: "https://climateos.co"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
keywords:
  - digital MRV
  - Internet of Things
  - blockchain
  - data provenance
  - renewable energy
  - carbon accounting
abstract: >-
  Signed solar-generation readings from ESP32 sensors are checked for
  authenticity and physical plausibility, allocated into one-tonne CO2
  impact records with self-verifying certificates on IPFS, and settled on
  Polygon Amoy. A prototype, not an accredited crediting programme.
